WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.269
Custom hook lesson

1
00:00:02.359 --> 00:00:03.579
What is a custom hook?

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:08.279
A custom hook in React is a JavaScript function that starts with use

3
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.140
and can call other hooks.

4
00:00:10.359 --> 00:00:13.880
It is used to extract component logic into reusable functions.

5
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.719
Why do we use custom hooks?

6
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.909
Custom hooks allow you to reuse stateful logic between different components.

7
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.979
They are useful for sharing logic that may be repetitive

8
00:00:31.309 --> 00:00:33.090
across multiple components.

9
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.619
They help to reduce code duplication

10
00:00:35.799 --> 00:00:38.840
and improve the maintainability of your react applications.

11
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:40.909
Basic syntax.

12
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.880
Here's how you define a simple custom hook.

13
00:00:45.419 --> 00:00:45.720
First,

14
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:46.900
declare,

15
00:00:47.529 --> 00:00:50.720
function use my custom hook open parenthesis,

16
00:00:51.159 --> 00:00:52.299
close parenthesis.

17
00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.200
Inside the function,

18
00:00:54.819 --> 00:00:57.439
declare cons state and set state

19
00:00:57.659 --> 00:00:59.659
using use state set to null.

20
00:01:00.349 --> 00:01:02.229
Add more logic here as needed.

21
00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:03.750
Finally,

22
00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:05.180
return state

23
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.559
and set state.

24
